> So the bug was that your system was not configured correctly!?

Yes it was, but nethack WILL run without compression. The save files just
will be stored uncompressed.

> I won't say so. How could Nethack load existing save files if the link to
> the compression program is broken after the files have been saved?

It works, because they aren't stored compressed, if compression failed when
saving the file, because of the missing compression executable.

> I see the bug in the misconfigured Nethack/OS pack.

It is one bug yes, however it triggered another bug.

> It makes sense to terminate the process with a failure exit code and clean
> any ressources of the spawned process if some system call fails.

Yes but here is the problem, the child process does not just clean ub any
resources of the spawned process, but also the resources of the parent
process. However the parent process want to continue running!

 
> Do you say here that Nethack, if it cannot decompress a compressed save
> file, will start a new game? (That would be not the worst behaviour, IMO.)

That okay, the parent process tries so, HOWEVER AGAIN, the child process
cleaned everything up. So it fails, segfaults, or hangs up. (In case of
falconseye, it child closes all window resources.

I am saying to be more exactly, the child should terminate with
exit(EXIT_FAILURE); not with terminate(EXIT_FAILURE), it's one line to be
replaced. Since it just has to exit, nothing more, it has NOT to clean
anything up, since the parent doesnt want to, runs further, if the parent
decides to give it. IT should then teminate(EXIT_FAILURE), and clean
everything up. NOT the child.

I know the bug is not triggered when the compression executable is
available, however it is triggered if it isn't. It isn't a major bug, or a
stopper, but it is a minor flaw that could, so believe I, be rather fixed
simply by changing this one line.

